@startuml
title Client Channel Authorisation with Keycloak
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

participant "RaftClient" as C
participant "Keycloak\n(realm)" as K
box "Raft node" #F6F6F6
participant "ClientAuthInterceptor" as I
participant "KeycloakTokenVerifier" as V
participant "RaftClientGrpcService" as S
end box

== Token (service account, cached until shortly before expiry) ==
C -> K: POST .../openid-connect/token\n(client_credentials)
K --> C: access_token (JWT, RS256)

== First request: realm keys are fetched once ==
C -> I: Submit(cmd)\nauthorization: Bearer <token>
I -> V: verify(token)
V -> K: GET .../openid-connect/certs
K --> V: JWK set (cached)
V -> V: signature (RS256 only)\nissuer, expiry, audience
V --> I: AuthenticatedClient(subject, roles)
I -> I: Submit needs 'raft-write'
I -> S: Submit(cmd)
S --> C: SubmitResponse

== Later requests: no call to Keycloak ==
C -> I: AddServer(n4)\nauthorization: Bearer <token>
I -> V: verify(token)
V --> I: AuthenticatedClient(subject, roles)
I -> I: AddServer needs 'raft-admin'
I --> C: PERMISSION_DENIED\n(role 'raft-admin' is required)
note over S: never reached

== No or invalid token ==
C -> I: Query(q)
I --> C: UNAUTHENTICATED
@enduml
